<DocsLayout
  title="How BudgetBaby Works"
  description="How BudgetBaby thinks about Safe to Spend, Money Pools, priority colors, period mechanics, and the design choices behind the local-first model."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/core-concepts"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>How BudgetBaby Works</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      BudgetBaby is built around one insight: most budgeting apps tell you how much you have spent
      but not how much you can safely spend right now. This page explains the connected systems that
      answer that question, and the reasoning behind each design choice.
    </p>

    <h2 id="safe-to-spend">Safe to Spend</h2>
    <p>
      The home screen is organized around one number: Safe to Spend. It answers the question every
      budgeter needs answered before every purchase:
      <em>"How much can I spend today without breaking my budget?"</em>
    </p>
    <p>
      This is different from "How much do I have left?" because <em>left</em> doesn't account for
      how many days remain in the period, upcoming bills you haven't paid, or money you intended to
      save. Safe to Spend rolls all of that in and produces a per-day allowance.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Home. Comfortable" caption="Daily rate is at or above 80% of the per-day budget. Spend confidently.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-bar-title" style="font-size:11px;">Home</span><span class="dm-bar-action">+</span></div>
