    <h2 id="pools-in-practice">Pools in practice</h2>
    <p>Here's how a typical credit card purchase cycle looks in BudgetBaby:</p>
    <div class="concept-example">
      <div class="ce-header">Grocery run on a credit card</div>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>You buy $120 of groceries.</strong> Log it as $120 Credit, category "Groceries" (yellow / Variable). Credit shows −$120. Debit is unchanged. Safe to Spend drops by $120 ÷ days remaining.</li>
        <li><strong>You pay your credit card bill.</strong> Log a transfer: $120 from Debit to Credit. Debit drops by $120. Credit returns to $0. Net: Debit is $120 lower, reflecting the real money that left your bank.</li>
        <li><strong>End result.</strong> Insights shows $120 spent on Groceries. Debit pool correctly reflects that $120 left your account when you paid the bill.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Cash and Debit balances carry forward between periods automatically.</strong> At the
      end of every period, the current Cash and Debit balances become the starting balances for
      the next period.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Credit purchase" caption="Logged as Credit, lowers Safe to Spend, leaves Debit untouched.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-bar-title" style="font-size:11px;">Trader Joe's</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Edit</span></div>
